#!/usr/bin/env bash
# check-shipped-language.sh — the shipped-artifact language gate (SPEC INV-120, ROADMAP row 275;
# composes with row 274's impersonal voice). Refuses a shipped file that carries Cyrillic outside
# a deliberate user-language string, or an owner/personal name, reporting each as file:line.
# The engine (Unicode-robust, allowlist-aware) is scripts/check-shipped-language.py.
set -euo pipefail
REPO_ROOT="${1:-$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)}"
cd "$REPO_ROOT"
exec python3 "$REPO_ROOT/scripts/check-shipped-language.py" --root "$REPO_ROOT"
=== doc-bounds ===
{
  "_comment": "The growable-doc bounds (SPEC INV-234, ROADMAP row 392). Each of the four large working documents declares a byte ceiling with a recorded reason; the watcher guardrails/check-doc-bound.py (gate z) reds a doc past its ceiling with no rotation dated today and no raised bound. It composes with the doc-rotation gate (gate t, INV-209): crossing the bound earns a rotation, and rotation is the remedy the red points to. Each ceiling is seeded ABOVE the current file size with roughly a hundred kilobytes of rotation headroom (measured 2026-07-18: PRODUCT_SPEC ~599 KB, ROADMAP ~603 KB, TEST_MATRIX ~345 KB, JOURNAL ~543 KB), so this gate never reds the already-large tree; the ceiling rises only with a recorded reason edited into this file, and rotation resets the live file well back under it. Bytes are the honest signal for the owner's cost — a guard's scan and a grep run slow with file size, named in kilobytes at ~18:25 on 2026-07-17.",
  "docs": {
    "PRODUCT_SPEC.md": {
      "max_bytes": 840000,
      "reason": "raised 2026-07-20 for the back-describe migration (v3.0.0, INV-239/INV-217): the Formal index gained a permanent Description column giving every registered code its plain-description line (~91 KB: 642 KB to 736 KB), taking the live file to ~736 KB; the ceiling sits above that with rotation headroom, and the closed portion still rotates before it is neared."
    },
    "ROADMAP.md": {
      "max_bytes": 700000,
      "reason": "the queue rotates by the closing-commit law (SPEC INV-276, ROADMAP row 480), not the milestone batch: a row reaching a terminal exit moves to that month's archive docs/queue-archive/rotated-ROADMAP-YYYY-MM.md in the same commit that closes it, so the live body stays the live queue and the byte ceiling is only a backstop. The number is held this stage above the ~603 KB current with rotation headroom; it ratchets down in the conversion stage, once the body actually shrinks to its live rows."
    },
    "TEST_MATRIX.md": {
      "max_bytes": 530000,
      "reason": "seed 2026-07-18 above ~345 KB current with rotation headroom; closed-row matrix entries rotate before this ceiling. Raised 2026-07-28 on a measurement over the live document: TEST_MATRIX.md carries 472 body rows — 431 read *built*, 41 read *todo*, 0 read *retired*. Zero rows carry an anchor that has left PRODUCT_SPEC.md and ARCHITECTURE.md, so a rotation moving every archivable row would move zero rows and free no meaningful bytes. The document grew because the product's covered surface grew, not because stale rows sit waiting to rotate, so rotation is the wrong remedy and the ceiling is the number that was stale. The ceiling rises to 530000, keeping the file's own convention of roughly a hundred kilobytes of headroom above the current size; rotation stays the remedy once closed rows exist to move."
    },
    "JOURNAL.md": {
      "max_bytes": 640000,
      "reason": "seed 2026-07-18 above ~543 KB current with rotation headroom; old dated chapters rotate to a dated archive before this ceiling."
    }
  }
}
=== size-ratchet ===
{
  "_comment": "The size ratchet for PRODUCT_SPEC.md (SPEC INV-264). The bound is bytes-per-criterion: the byte count of the spec's criterion lines alone (glossary and preamble excluded) divided by the count of criteria in its body. A delivery may lower it or leave it; no delivery may raise it (raising is a change to Requirement 4, INV-265). The ratchet governs PRODUCT_SPEC.md only; the other documents keep their flat byte bound (check-doc-bound.py).",
  "governs": "PRODUCT_SPEC.md",
  "bytes_per_criterion": 207.2,
  "reason": "Seeded at the row-445 spec-format migration-end freeze and lowered by the freeze actor at the pass-2 re-baseline (206.9 over 1360 criteria; the pass-1 seed was 209.0 over 1301). Re-baselined up at the row-456 architecture-format landing to 207.2 (measured 207.196 over 1420 criteria): six behavioral rules relocated from ARCHITECTURE.md owns cells into their spec clauses (INV-279) — the runaway-child fire-timing, the perms-arm settings scope and glob/spaced-path parsing and unreadable stand-down, the hedge-gate personal overlay, the read-grant profile field, and the node-growth and expensive-decision push status — plus the three architecture-format requirements 289-291. The companion move shed 31 KB from ARCHITECTURE.md, so the system's total content fell while the spec's criterion density rose. This raise is the deliberate Requirement-4 change INV-265 requires; a later delivery may lower this bound or leave it, and none may raise it without the same justification (INV-264, INV-265)."
}

